/*  Functions — `Bind`, `Return` and `cast`: `Pass1Hoist`'s free functions, `CheckBindBody`,
    `CheckReturn`, `ResolveForCast` and `ValidateCastArgs` in `src/Interpreter/TypeChecker.*.cs`.

    ★ A function's type is `(FunctionType [parameter types] <return type or _> [parameter names])`.
    The names ride along because a call may NAME its arguments, and a function reached through a
    value keeps the names of the declaration it came from; a type written in an annotation has no
    names, and such a call cannot name them. The names are not part of the type's identity.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    /// A function's type, as a declaration gives it.
    Bind node to function-type-of, given (the node statement):
        Define parameter-types as cast listed.
        Define parameter-names as cast listed.
        For each parameter in (cast field-of on (statement, 3))'s children, repeat:
            Cast parameter-types's add on (cast field-of on (parameter, 1)).
            Cast parameter-names's add on (cast field-of on (parameter, 2)).
        Done.
        Define shape as cast plain-type on ("FunctionType").
        Cast shape's add on (parameter-types).
        Cast shape's add on (cast signature-return on (statement)).
        Cast shape's add on (parameter-names).
        Return shape.
    Done.

    /// The names a function's parameters are called, or nothing when its type was written.
    Bind voidable series of text to parameter-names-of, given (the node shape):
        If the number of shape's children is less than 3, return void.
        Define names as a series of text.
        For each named in (cast field-of on (shape, 3))'s children, repeat:
            Insert cast unquoted on (named) into names.
        Done.
        Return names.
    Done.

    Bind fact to is-bundled-module, given (the text name):
        Return cast is-a-book on (name) or name is "rabbit".
    Done.

    // ── What this checker can judge in a function ─────────────────────────

    /// Why this `Bind` is beyond reach yet, or "".
    Bind text to bind-beyond-reach, given (the node statement):
        If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 5)) is false, return "a method bound 'unto' a type".
        // A function lowered from an axiom is an ordinary one; any other mark is beyond reach yet.
        Define place as 9.
        While place is less than the number of statement's children, repeat:
            Define mark as (cast field-of on (statement, place))'s word.
            If mark is not ":FromAxiomLanguage", return "a Bind with {mark}".
            Increment place by 2.
        Done.
        Define returned as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
        If cast is-nothing on (returned) is false:
            If cast beyond-types on (returned):
                Return "a function giving back a {returned's kind}".
            Done.
        Done.
        For each parameter in (cast field-of on (statement, 3))'s children, repeat:
            Define taken as cast field-of on (parameter, 1).
            If cast beyond-types on (taken):
                Return "a function taking a {taken's kind}".
            Done.
        Done.
        Return cast beyond-reach on (cast field-of on (statement, 4)).
    Done.

    // ── Versions of one name ──────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// `DispatchExpansion`, which runs before anything is gathered: top-level functions that share
    /// a name are versions of it. Only its refusals are here — a group that really does dispatch,
    /// or carries a `when`, is beyond this checker yet.
    Bind void or failure to check-versions, given (the node program):
        Define order as a series of text.
        Define groups as a map from text to node.
        For each statement in program's children, repeat:
            If statement's kind is "BindStatement" and cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 5)):
                Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
                Define group as the entry for name in groups.
                If group is void:
                    Define fresh-group as cast listed.
                    In groups, the entry for name becomes fresh-group.
                    Insert name into order.
                    Cast fresh-group's add on (statement).
                Done.
                Otherwise:
                    Cast group's add on (statement).
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        For each name in order, repeat:
            Define versions as (the entry for name in groups but void is cast listed)'s children.
            Define first as item 1 of versions.
            If the number of versions is greater than 1:
                Define first-count as the number of (cast field-of on (first, 3))'s children.
                Define first-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (first, 7)).
                Define place as 0.
                For each other in versions, repeat:
                    Increment place by 1.
                    If place is greater than 1:
                        Define other-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (other, 7)).
                        Define other-count as the number of (cast field-of on (other, 3))'s children.
                        If other-count is not first-count:
                            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("the versions of '{name}' take different numbers of arguments",
                                "The one on line {first-row} takes {first-count}, and this one takes {other-count}",
                                other-row, "declare a version of '{name}' with a different number of arguments",
                                "Every version of a name is reached by the same call, so they all take the same arguments. Rename this one if it does something else.")).
                        Done.
                        Define first-gives as cast field-of on (first, 2).
                        Define other-gives as cast field-of on (other, 2).
                        If cast type-key on (first-gives) is not cast type-key on (other-gives):
                            Define first-said as "nothing".
                            If cast is-nothing on (first-gives) is false, the first-said becomes cast type-words on (first-gives).
                            Define other-said as "nothing".
                            If cast is-nothing on (other-gives) is false, the other-said becomes cast type-words on (other-gives).
                            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("the versions of '{name}' give back different types",
                                "The one on line {first-row} gives back {first-said}, and this one gives back {other-said}",
                                other-row, "declare a version of '{name}' with another return type",
                                "A caller has to know what it gets back without knowing which version ran, so every version gives back the same type.")).
                        Done.
                    Done.
                Done.
                // Versions with the same argument types and no condition cannot be told apart.
                Define fallbacks as a map from text to number.
                For each version in versions, repeat:
                    If cast has-mark on (version, ":When"):
                        Return a failure (cast not-judged on ("a version of '{name}' with a condition")).
                    Done.
                    Define key as cast type-key on (cast parameter-types-of on (version)).
                    Define version-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (version, 7)).
                    Define already as the entry for key in fallbacks.
                    If already is not void:
                        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' is declared twice with the same argument types",
                            "It was already declared on line {already}", version-row,
                            "declare '{name}' again with nothing to tell the two apart",
                            "Versions of a name are told apart by one argument's type or by a 'when' condition. These have neither, so no call could pick between them. Rename one of them.")).
                    Done.
                    In fallbacks, the entry for key becomes version-row.
                Done.
                Return a failure (cast not-judged on ("versions of '{name}' told apart by type")).
            Done.
            If cast has-mark on (first, ":When"):
                Return a failure (cast not-judged on ("a version of '{name}' with a condition")).
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// A function's parameter types, as one list.
    Bind node to parameter-types-of, given (the node statement):
        Define types as cast listed.
        For each parameter in (cast field-of on (statement, 3))'s children, repeat:
            Cast types's add on (cast field-of on (parameter, 1)).
        Done.
        Return types.
    Done.

    // ── Blanks ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// Does this name already mean a type — an object, an interface, or one a book introduces?
    Bind fact to is-known-type-name unto checker, given (the text name):
        If (the entry for name in one's defs) is not void, return true.
        If (the entry for name in one's generic-defs) is not void, return true.
        If cast one's is-interface-name on (name), return true.
        Return cast book-introducing on (name) is not "".
    Done.

    Bind void to count-unknown-names unto checker, given (the node shape, the map from text to number counts):
        If shape's kind is "ObjectType":
            Define arguments-given as cast field-of on (shape, 2).
            If arguments-given's kind is "list" and the number of arguments-given's children is 0:
                Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (shape, 1)).
                If cast one's is-known-type-name on (name) is false:
                    In counts, the entry for name becomes (the entry for name in counts but void is 0) + 1.
                Done.
            Done.
            If arguments-given's kind is "list":
                For each inner in arguments-given's children, repeat:
                    Cast one's count-unknown-names on (inner, counts).
                Done.
            Done.
            Return.
        Done.
        For each inner in shape's children, repeat:
            If inner's kind is not "atom", cast one's count-unknown-names on (inner, counts).
        Done.
    Done.

    /// A signature's BLANKS — unknown type names written at least twice (`SignatureBlanks`). Twice
    /// is what keeps a typo a typo: a misspelling written once stays an unknown type.
    Bind fact to has-blanks unto checker, given (the node statement):
        Define counts as a map from text to number.
        For each parameter in (cast field-of on (statement, 3))'s children, repeat:
            Cast one's count-unknown-names on (cast field-of on (parameter, 1), counts).
        Done.
        Define returned as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
        If cast is-nothing on (returned) is false, cast one's count-unknown-names on (returned, counts).
        For each pair in counts, repeat:
            If the value of pair is greater than 1, return true.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    // ── Gathering them first ──────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// Every top-level function, in scope before anything is checked — so one may call another
    /// declared further down. Two with one name are refused, the second pointing at the first.
    Bind void or failure to hoist-functions unto checker, given (the node program):
        Define seen as a map from text to number.
        For each statement in cast hoistable on (program), repeat:
            If statement's kind is "BindStatement" and cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 5)):
                Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
                Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 7)).
                Define earlier as the entry for name in seen.
                If earlier is not void:
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' is declared twice",
                        "It was already declared on line {earlier}", at-row, "declare '{name}' again",
                        "Two functions cannot share a name — the second would silently replace the first. Rename one of them.")).
                Done.
                In seen, the entry for name becomes at-row.
                Cast check-buries-say-what on (statement, "function") or pass the failure off.
                // A function that leaves blanks is a template: set aside, checked only per filling.
                If cast one's has-blanks on (statement):
                    In one's templates, the entry for name becomes true.
                    In one's generic-binds, the entry for name becomes statement.
                    Skip.
                Done.
                Define hoisted-return as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
                If cast is-nothing on (hoisted-return) is false:
                    Cast one's check-resolves on (hoisted-return) or pass the failure off.
                Done.
                Cast one's bind-name on (name, a new binding {
                    the shape cast function-type-of on (statement),
                    the established-by cast named-reference on (name), the line at-row, the permanent false, the module false, the depth 0, the parameter false }).
                // So a pipe can check this body again once it knows what flows into it.
                In one's free-binds, the entry for name becomes statement.
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    // ── A function's body ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// A pulled module is a capability of the block it is pulled in, so a body written there has it.
    Bind void to carry-modules, given (the series of map from text to binding saved, the map from text to binding fresh):
        For each scope in saved, repeat:
            For each pair in scope, repeat:
                Define held as the value of pair.
                If held's module or held's shape's kind is "BookType":
                    In fresh, the entry for (the key of pair) becomes held.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// The type scopes back to how many there were — a body's own scope is left, not exited.
    Bind void to trim-type-scopes unto checker, given (the number kept):
        While the number of one's type-scopes is greater than kept, repeat:
            Remove item (the number of one's type-scopes) from one's type-scopes.
        Done.
    Done.

    Bind void or failure to check-bind-statement unto checker, given (the node statement):
        Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
        Define target as cast field-of on (statement, 5).
        If cast is-nothing on (target) is false:
            // Aimed at a template or a filling, it was folded into that type and is checked there.
            If cast one's is-absorbed on (cast unquoted on (target)), return.
            // The object is `one`, and the line it is said to be made on is the method's own.
            Cast one's check-method-body on (statement, cast unquoted on (target),
                cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 7))) or pass the failure off.
            Return.
        Done.
        If (the entry for name in one's templates) is not void, return.
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 7)).
        // A top-level function is in scope already, from the hoist; a nested one arrives here.
        If (the entry for name in cast one's innermost) is void:
            Cast one's bind-name on (name, a new binding {
                the shape cast function-type-of on (statement),
                the established-by cast named-reference on (name), the line at-row, the permanent false, the module false, the depth 0, the parameter false }).
        Done.
        Define filled-origin as the entry for name in one's origins.
        If filled-origin is not void:
            Try to:
                Cast one's check-bind-body on (statement).
            Done.
            In case of failure:
                Return a failure (cast filled-body-refused on (filled-origin, the message of the failure)).
            Done.
            Return.
        Done.
        Cast one's check-bind-body on (statement) or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    /// What a body sees: its parameters, and — from the top level — functions and `permanently`
    /// constants only; top-level data it may not read. A function inside another sees all of it.
    Bind void or failure to check-bind-body unto checker, given (the node statement):
        Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
        Define returned as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 7)).
        // Lowered from an axiom, it still owes the pull its language wants around it.
        Define axiom-language as cast bind-mark on (statement, ":FromAxiomLanguage").
        If axiom-language is not "", cast one's require-language-pulled on (axiom-language, at-row) or pass the failure off.

        Define saved as one's scopes.
        Define saved-types as the number of one's type-scopes.
        Define fresh as cast builtin-scope.
        Cast carry-modules on (saved, fresh).
        Define earlier-hidden as one's hidden.
        Define nested as one's in-function.
        If nested:
            For each scope in saved, repeat:
                For each pair in scope, repeat:
                    Define held as the value of pair.
                    If held's parameter and cast is-reference-type on (held's shape):
                        In fresh, the entry for (the key of pair) becomes a new binding {
                            the shape held's shape, the established-by held's established-by, the line held's line,
                            the permanent held's permanent, the module held's module,
                            the depth cast captured-parameter-depth, the parameter true }.
                    Done.
                    Otherwise:
                        In fresh, the entry for (the key of pair) becomes held.
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        Otherwise:
            Define hiding as a map from text to fact.
            For each scope in saved, repeat:
                For each pair in scope, repeat:
                    Define held as the value of pair.
                    If held's shape's kind is "FunctionType" or held's permanent:
                        In fresh, the entry for (the key of pair) becomes held.
                    Done.
                    Otherwise:
                        In hiding, the entry for (the key of pair) becomes true.
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
            The one's hidden becomes hiding.
        Done.
        The one's scopes becomes a series with (fresh).
        Cast one's enter-scope.
        For each parameter in (cast field-of on (statement, 3))'s children, repeat:
            Define parameter-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (parameter, 2)).
            Cast one's check-resolves on (cast field-of on (parameter, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's bind-name on (parameter-name, a new binding {
                the shape cast one's resolved on (cast field-of on (parameter, 1)),
                the established-by cast named-reference on (parameter-name), the line at-row, the permanent false, the module false, the depth 0, the parameter true }).
        Done.

        Define earlier-in-function as one's in-function.
        Define earlier-line as one's function-line.
        Define earlier-depth as one's rabbit-depth.
        The one's rabbit-depth becomes 0.
        Increment one's nesting by 1.
        The one's in-function becomes true.
        // One per body entered, so leaving it is taking the last one off.
        If cast is-nothing on (returned), insert cast unknown-type into one's expected-returns.
        Otherwise, insert cast one's resolved on (returned) into one's expected-returns.
        The one's function-line becomes at-row.

        Define earlier-recording as one's recording-stash.
        The one's recording-stash becomes "".
        If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 5)) and cast contains-bury on (cast field-of on (statement, 4)):
            The one's recording-stash becomes name.
        Done.
        Cast one's check-block on (cast field-of on (statement, 4)) or pass the failure off.
        The one's recording-stash becomes earlier-recording.

        The one's in-function becomes earlier-in-function.
        Remove item (the number of one's expected-returns) from one's expected-returns.
        The one's function-line becomes earlier-line.
        The one's rabbit-depth becomes earlier-depth.
        Decrement one's nesting by 1.
        The one's hidden becomes earlier-hidden.
        The one's scopes becomes saved.
        Cast one's trim-type-scopes on (saved-types).

        If cast is-nothing on (returned) is false and cast is-void-or-failure on (returned) is false
                and cast contains-bury on (cast field-of on (statement, 4)) is false
                and cast definitely-returns on (cast field-of on (statement, 4)) is false:
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (
                "'{name}' is declared to give back a {cast type-words on (returned)}, but it can reach its end without returning one", "",
                at-row, "define a function that might not return a value",
                "Make sure every path through the function ends with a return statement.")).
        Done.
    Done.

    /// `InferLambdaLiteral`: a function with no name. It CAPTURES its enclosing scope — all of it,
    /// at every level — and what it gives back is read off its first `Return`.
    Bind node or failure to infer-lambda unto checker, given (the node said):
        Define parameters as (cast field-of on (said, 1))'s children.
        Define body as cast field-of on (said, 2).
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (said, 3)).
        Cast refuse-burying-lambda on (body) or pass the failure off.
        // Its statements sit inside an expression, out of sight of the program's own pre-scan.
        Define inner-reach as cast beyond-reach on (body).
        If inner-reach is not "", return a failure (cast not-judged on (inner-reach)).

        Define saved as one's scopes.
        Define saved-types as the number of one's type-scopes.
        Define fresh as cast builtin-scope.
        For each scope in saved, repeat:
            For each pair in scope, repeat:
                Define held as the value of pair.
                If held's parameter and cast is-reference-type on (held's shape):
                    In fresh, the entry for (the key of pair) becomes a new binding {
                        the shape held's shape, the established-by held's established-by, the line held's line,
                        the permanent held's permanent, the module held's module,
                        the depth cast captured-parameter-depth, the parameter true }.
                Done.
                Otherwise:
                    In fresh, the entry for (the key of pair) becomes held.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        The one's scopes becomes a series with (fresh).
        Cast one's enter-scope.
        Define parameter-types as cast listed.
        Define parameter-names as cast listed.
        For each parameter in parameters, repeat:
            Define parameter-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (parameter, 2)).
            Cast one's check-resolves on (cast field-of on (parameter, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            Define taken as cast one's resolved on (cast field-of on (parameter, 1)).
            Cast parameter-types's add on (taken).
            Cast parameter-names's add on (cast field-of on (parameter, 2)).
            Cast one's bind-name on (parameter-name, a new binding {
                the shape taken, the established-by cast named-reference on (parameter-name), the line at-row,
                the permanent false, the module false, the depth 0, the parameter true }).
        Done.

        Define earlier-in-function as one's in-function.
        Define earlier-line as one's function-line.
        Define earlier-depth as one's rabbit-depth.
        Define earlier-inferring as one's inferring-lambda.
        Define earlier-fallible as one's overload-fallible.
        The one's rabbit-depth becomes 0.
        Increment one's nesting by 1.
        The one's in-function becomes true.
        The one's inferring-lambda becomes true.
        The one's overload-fallible becomes false.
        Insert cast unknown-type into one's expected-returns.
        The one's function-line becomes at-row.

        Define earlier-recording as one's recording-stash.
        The one's recording-stash becomes "".
        Cast one's check-block on (body) or pass the failure off.
        The one's recording-stash becomes earlier-recording.

        Define inferred as item (the number of one's expected-returns) of one's expected-returns.
        Remove item (the number of one's expected-returns) from one's expected-returns.
        The one's in-function becomes earlier-in-function.
        The one's inferring-lambda becomes earlier-inferring.
        The one's overload-fallible becomes earlier-fallible.
        The one's function-line becomes earlier-line.
        The one's rabbit-depth becomes earlier-depth.
        Decrement one's nesting by 1.
        The one's scopes becomes saved.
        Cast one's trim-type-scopes on (saved-types).

        If cast is-none on (inferred) is false and cast definitely-returns on (body) is false:
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (
                "this lambda is inferred to give back a {cast type-words on (inferred)}, but it can reach its end without returning one", "",
                at-row, "write a lambda that might not return a value",
                "Make sure every path through the lambda ends with a return statement.")).
        Done.
        Define shape as cast plain-type on ("FunctionType").
        Cast shape's add on (parameter-types).
        If cast is-none on (inferred), cast shape's add on (cast nothing).
        Otherwise, cast shape's add on (inferred).
        Cast shape's add on (parameter-names).
        Return shape.
    Done.

    Bind void or failure to check-return unto checker, given (the node statement):
        Define value as cast field-of on (statement, 1).
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)).
        // The first `Return` of a lambda says what the lambda gives back.
        If one's inferring-lambda:
            Define handed as cast unknown-type.
            If cast is-nothing on (value) is false, the handed becomes cast one's infer on (value) or pass the failure off.
            If one's overload-fallible:
                If handed's kind is "FailureMarkerType", return.
                If cast is-nothing on (value) is false:
                    If cast is-failure-expression on (value), return.
                Done.
                If cast is-none on (handed) is false:
                    Define as-fallible as cast plain-type on ("FailureType").
                    Cast as-fallible's add on (handed).
                    The handed becomes as-fallible.
                Done.
            Done.
            The item (the number of one's expected-returns) of one's expected-returns becomes handed.
            The one's inferring-lambda becomes false.
            Return.
        Done.
        Define expected as item (the number of one's expected-returns) of one's expected-returns.
        Define gives-value as cast is-nothing on (value) is false.
        If cast is-none on (expected):
            If gives-value and value's kind is "FailureLiteral":
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("this function is declared void, so it cannot give back a failure", "",
                    at-row, "return a failure from it",
                    "If it is meant to be able to fail, say so where it is declared: 'Bind void or failure to …'.")).
            Done.
            If gives-value:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("this function is declared void — it gives nothing back", "",
                    at-row, "return a value from a void function",
                    "Remove the value, or change the function's return type if you need to produce a result.")).
            Done.
            Return.
        Done.
        If cast is-void-or-failure on (expected):
            If gives-value:
                Define handed as cast one's infer on (value) or pass the failure off.
                If cast is-failure-expression on (value) is false and handed's kind is not "FailureMarkerType"
                        and cast is-void-or-failure on (handed) is false:
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("this function is declared 'void or failure' — when it works it gives nothing back",
                        "You declared the return type on line {one's function-line}", at-row, "return a value from it",
                        "Write 'Return.' for success, or 'Return a failure \"…\".' when it does not work.")).
                Done.
            Done.
            Return.
        Done.
        Define promised as cast type-words on (expected).
        Define declared-on as "You declared the return type as {promised} on line {one's function-line}".
        If gives-value is false:
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("this function is declared to give back a {promised}", declared-on,
                at-row, "return without a value", "Provide a {promised} value to return.")).
        Done.
        Define value-type as cast unknown-type.
        If cast is-none on (cast one's axiom-behind on (value)) is false and expected's kind is not "AxiomType":
            The value-type becomes cast one's run-axiom-on-return on (value, at-row) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise:
            The value-type becomes cast one's infer on (value) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        // Running needs the source, which a parameter or another call's result does not carry.
        If value-type's kind is "AxiomType" and expected's kind is not "AxiomType":
            Return a failure (cast source-not-reachable on (value-type, at-row)).
        Done.
        If cast is-rabbit-type on (value-type):
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("rabbits cannot be returned — they flow downward only", "",
                at-row, "return a rabbit from a function",
                "Pass the rabbit as an argument instead, or return a value that lives in it (a handle into the rabbit).")).
        Done.
        If cast is-none on (value-type), return.
        If cast assignable on (expected, value-type), return.
        If cast beyond-types on (value-type), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("returning a {value-type's kind}")).
        If value's kind is "FailureLiteral":
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("this function is declared to give back a {promised}, and a failure is not one",
                declared-on, at-row, "return a failure from it",
                "If it is meant to be able to fail, say so where it is declared: 'Bind {promised} or failure to …'.")).
        Done.
        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("this function is declared to give back a {promised}", declared-on,
            at-row, "return a {cast type-words on (value-type)} value", "Change the returned value to a {promised}.")).
    Done.

    // ── Calls ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// What `cast f on (…)` reaches: the function's type, how a refusal names it, and the line it
    /// was declared on. Gives back a `call` — or `none` for a callee whose type is not known.
    Define object call with (the node shape, the text display, the number declared-on, the number receivers).

    Bind call or failure to resolve-cast unto checker, given (the node callee, the node call-args,
            the number at-row, the text filled):
        If callee's kind is "VariableReference":
            Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (callee, 1)).
            // A filling is registered under its filled name; the name written is the template's.
            Define called as name.
            If filled is not "", the called becomes filled.
            // ⚠ The first argument is typed BEFORE the name is looked up: C# asks it whether the
            // call is a method on an object, and a refusal inside it comes first.
            Define dispatched as cast unknown-type.
            Define owner as "".
            If the number of call-args's children is greater than 0:
                Define first as cast one's infer on (item 1 of call-args's children) or pass the failure off.
                If cast beyond-types on (first), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("a call whose first argument is a {first's kind}")).
                If first's kind is "ObjectType":
                    The owner becomes cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (first, 1)).
                    If cast one's definition-of on (owner) is void, return a failure (cast not-judged on ("a call on a '{owner}'")).
                    Define method as cast one's method-type-of on (owner, called).
                    If method is not void, the dispatched becomes method.
                Done.
                If first's kind is "InterfaceType":
                    Define interface-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (first, 1)).
                    Define reached-method as cast one's interface-method-named on (interface-name, name).
                    If reached-method is not void:
                        Define found-too as cast one's look-up on (name).
                        If found-too is not void:
                            If found-too's shape's kind is "FunctionType":
                                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' is both a method and a free function — this is ambiguous", "",
                                    at-row, "call '{name}' ambiguously",
                                    "Use the possessive form to call the method explicitly: Cast <object>'s {name} on (args).")).
                            Done.
                        Done.
                        Return a new call { the shape reached-method, the display "method '{name}' on interface '{interface-name}'",
                            the declared-on at-row, the receivers 1 }.
                    Done.
                    If cast one's look-up on (name) is void:
                        Define offered as cast one's interface-method-names on (interface-name).
                        Define fix as "Interface '{interface-name}' declares no methods.".
                        If the number of offered is greater than 0, the fix becomes "Available methods: {cast quoted-names on (offered, "")}.".
                        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("interface '{interface-name}' has no method named '{name}'", "",
                            at-row, "call method '{name}' through interface '{interface-name}'", fix)).
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
            Define found as cast one's look-up on (called).
            If cast is-none on (dispatched) is false:
                If found is not void:
                    If found's shape's kind is "FunctionType":
                        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' is both a method and a free function — this is ambiguous", "",
                            at-row, "call '{name}' ambiguously",
                            "Use the possessive form to call the method explicitly: Cast <object>'s {name} on (args).")).
                    Done.
                Done.
                Return a new call { the shape dispatched, the display "method '{called}' on '{owner}'", the declared-on at-row, the receivers 1 }.
            Done.
            If found is void and owner is not "":
                Define methods as cast one's own-method-names on (owner).
                Define fix as "'{owner}' has no methods.".
                If the number of methods is greater than 0, the fix becomes "Available methods: {cast quoted-names on (methods, "")}.".
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{owner}' has no method named '{name}'", "",
                    at-row, "call method '{name}' on a {owner}", fix)).
            Done.
            If found is void:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' isn't defined, so there is nothing to cast",
                    "A cast reaches a function, a method, or an axiom, and no declaration of this name was found",
                    at-row, "cast '{name}'",
                    "Check the spelling, or declare it: 'Bind <type> to {name}, given (…):'.")).
            Done.
            If found's shape's kind is not "FunctionType":
                If cast beyond-types on (found's shape) or found's shape's kind is "AxiomType":
                    Return a failure (cast not-judged on ("casting a {found's shape's kind}")).
                Done.
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' holds a {cast type-words on (found's shape)}, not a function — you can only cast functions", "",
                    at-row, "cast something that isn't a function",
                    "Only functions can be cast. Make sure the name you're casting refers to a function.")).
            Done.
            Return a new call { the shape found's shape, the display "'{name}'", the declared-on found's line, the receivers 0 }.
        Done.
        Define reached as cast unknown-type.
        If callee's kind is "PossessiveAccess":
            Define looked-up as callee.
            If filled is not "", the looked-up becomes cast with-field on (callee, 2, cast quoted on (filled)).
            The reached becomes cast one's infer-possessive on (looked-up, true) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise:
            The reached becomes cast one's infer on (callee) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        If cast is-none on (reached):
            Return a new call { the shape reached, the display "this function", the declared-on at-row, the receivers 0 }.
        Done.
        If reached's kind is not "FunctionType":
            If cast beyond-types on (reached) or reached's kind is "AxiomType":
                Return a failure (cast not-judged on ("casting a {reached's kind}")).
            Done.
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("this expression holds a {cast type-words on (reached)}, not a function — you can only cast functions", "",
                at-row, "cast something that isn't a function", "Only functions can be cast.")).
        Done.
        Return a new call { the shape reached, the display "this function", the declared-on at-row, the receivers 0 }.
    Done.

    /// The arguments in the order the callee declares its parameters — `MergeNamedArgs`. A method
    /// called in the free form takes its object first, which is carried through and not named.
    Bind node or failure to merged-arguments unto checker, given (the node callee, the node positional,
            the node named, the number at-row):
        Define display as "this function".
        Define names as a series of text.
        Define known as false.
        Define receivers as 0.
        If callee's kind is "VariableReference":
            Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (callee, 1)).
            The display becomes "'{name}'".
            Define dispatched as false.
            Define first-owner as "".
            If the number of positional's children is greater than 0:
                Define first as cast one's infer on (item 1 of positional's children) or pass the failure off.
                If cast beyond-types on (first), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("named arguments after a {first's kind}")).
                If first's kind is "ObjectType":
                    The first-owner becomes cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (first, 1)).
                    Define method as cast one's method-type-of on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (first, 1)), name).
                    If method is not void:
                        The dispatched becomes true.
                        The receivers becomes 1.
                        The names becomes cast parameter-names-of on (method) but void is a series of text.
                        The known becomes true.
                    Done.
                Done.
                // Through an interface the parameters have no names, so none can be matched.
                If first's kind is "InterfaceType":
                    If cast one's interface-method-named on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (first, 1)), name) is not void:
                        The dispatched becomes true.
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
            If dispatched is false:
                Define found as cast one's look-up on (name).
                If found is not void:
                    If found's shape's kind is "FunctionType":
                        Define declared as cast parameter-names-of on (found's shape).
                        If declared is not void:
                            The names becomes declared.
                            The known becomes true.
                        Done.
                    Done.
                Done.
                // A template is reached before it is filled, and its parameters are declared.
                If known is false:
                    Define held as the entry for name in one's generic-binds.
                    If held is not void:
                        The names becomes cast parameter-names-of on (cast function-type-of on (held)) but void is a series of text.
                        The known becomes true.
                    Done.
                Done.
                If known is false and first-owner is not "":
                    Define held-method as the entry for "{first-owner}'s {name}" in one's generic-methods.
                    If held-method is not void:
                        The names becomes cast parameter-names-of on (cast function-type-of on (held-method)) but void is a series of text.
                        The receivers becomes 1.
                        The known becomes true.
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        Otherwise if callee's kind is "PossessiveAccess":
            Define member as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (callee, 2)).
            The display becomes "'{member}'".
            Define target as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (callee, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            If cast beyond-types on (target), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("named arguments to a method of a {target's kind}")).
            If target's kind is "ObjectType":
                // The type's own methods and its `unto` ones — not what it promotes.
                Define owner as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (target, 1)).
                Define definition as cast one's definition-of on (owner).
                If definition is not void:
                    For each method in cast one's all-methods on (definition), repeat:
                        If known is false and cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (method, 1)) is member
                                and cast one's is-nested-template on (method) is false:
                            The names becomes cast parameter-names-of on (cast function-type-of on (method)) but void is a series of text.
                            The known becomes true.
                        Done.
                    Done.
                    Define held-method as the entry for "{owner}'s {member}" in one's generic-methods.
                    If known is false:
                        If held-method is not void:
                            The names becomes cast parameter-names-of on (cast function-type-of on (held-method)) but void is a series of text.
                            The known becomes true.
                        Done.
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        Otherwise:
            Return a failure (cast not-judged on ("named arguments to a {callee's kind}")).
        Done.
        If known is false:
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("{display} can't be called with named arguments",
                "A name has to match a parameter the function DECLARES, and this call reaches its function through a value — a parameter, a field, or another call's result — which carries the parameter types but not what they are called",
                at-row, "name an argument here", "Pass the arguments in order instead.")).
        Done.

        Define slots as a map from number to node.
        Define filled as a map from number to text.
        Define kept as cast listed.
        Define place as 0.
        For each passed in positional's children, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            If place is greater than receivers:
                Define slot as place - receivers.
                If slot is greater than the number of names:
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("{display} takes {the number of names} argument(s), but you passed more", "",
                        at-row, "pass {the number of positional's children - receivers + the number of named's children} argument(s)",
                        "Remove the extra argument(s).")).
                Done.
                In slots, the entry for slot becomes passed.
                In filled, the entry for slot becomes "position".
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                Cast kept's add on (passed).
            Done.
        Done.
        For each pair in named's children, repeat:
            Define wanted as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (pair, 1)).
            Define slot as 0.
            Define tally as 0.
            For each candidate in names, repeat:
                Increment tally by 1.
                If slot is 0 and candidate is wanted, the slot becomes tally.
            Done.
            If slot is 0:
                Define listing as "It takes no parameters.".
                If the number of names is greater than 0:
                    The listing becomes "Its parameters are {cast quoted-names on (names, "")}.".
                Done.
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("{display} has no parameter called '{wanted}'", "",
                    at-row, "pass a value for '{wanted}'", listing)).
            Done.
            Define before as the entry for slot in filled but void is "".
            If before is "position":
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{wanted}' was already given as argument {slot + receivers}", "",
                    at-row, "give '{wanted}' twice", "Remove either the positional argument or 'the {wanted}'.")).
            Done.
            If before is "name":
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{wanted}' was given twice", "",
                    at-row, "give '{wanted}' twice", "Remove one of the two 'the {wanted}' arguments.")).
            Done.
            In slots, the entry for slot becomes cast field-of on (pair, 2).
            In filled, the entry for slot becomes "name".
        Done.
        Define tally as 0.
        For each candidate in names, repeat:
            Increment tally by 1.
            Define held as the entry for tally in slots.
            If held is void:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("{display} has no value for '{candidate}'", "",
                    at-row, "call {display} without a value for '{candidate}'",
                    "Add 'the {candidate} <value>', or pass it in position {tally}.")).
            Done.
            Cast kept's add on (held).
        Done.
        Return kept.
    Done.

    /// The arguments measured against the parameters — `ValidateCastArgs`.
    Bind void or failure to check-arguments unto checker, given (the call reached, the node call-args,
            the number at-row):
        Define formals as (cast field-of on (reached's shape, 1))'s children.
        Define supplied as a series of node.
        Define skipping as reached's receivers.
        For each passed in call-args's children, repeat:
            If skipping is greater than 0, decrement skipping by 1.
            Otherwise, insert passed into supplied.
        Done.
        Define display as reached's display.
        If the number of supplied is not the number of formals:
            Define advice as "Remove the extra argument(s).".
            If the number of supplied is less than the number of formals, the advice becomes "Add the missing argument(s).".
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (
                "{display} expects {the number of formals} argument(s), but you passed {the number of supplied}",
                "You declared it on line {reached's declared-on} with {the number of formals} parameter(s)",
                at-row, "call it with {the number of supplied} argument(s)", advice)).
        Done.
        Define place as 0.
        For each argument in supplied, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            Define argument-type as cast one's infer on (argument) or pass the failure off.
            Define formal as cast one's resolved on (item place of formals).
            If formal's kind is "InterfaceType" and cast is-none on (argument-type) is false:
                Cast one's check-interface-argument on (formal, argument-type, place, reached, at-row) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            Otherwise if cast is-none on (argument-type) is false and cast assignable on (formal, argument-type) is false:
                If cast beyond-types on (argument-type) or cast beyond-types on (formal):
                    Return a failure (cast not-judged on ("passing a {argument-type's kind}")).
                Done.
                If argument-type's kind is "VoidableType":
                    Define present as cast field-of on (argument-type, 1).
                    If cast assignable on (formal, present):
                        Return a failure (cast void-misuse on (argument,
                            "argument {place} of {display} needs a {cast type-words on (formal)} that is there",
                            "pass a {cast type-words on (argument-type)} as argument {place}",
                            "'{cast defaulted on (argument, present)}' in its place", at-row, "")).
                    Done.
                Done.
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (
                    "argument {place} of {display} must be a {cast type-words on (formal)}, but you passed a {cast type-words on (argument-type)}",
                    "You declared {display} on line {reached's declared-on}, so argument {place} must be a {cast type-words on (formal)}",
                    at-row, "pass a {cast type-words on (argument-type)} as argument {place}",
                    "Change argument {place} to a {cast type-words on (formal)}.")).
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// `cast f on (…)`, as a statement or a value. Gives back what it returns, or `none`.
    Bind node or failure to check-call unto checker, given (the node said, the fact as-value):
        Define callee as cast field-of on (said, 1).
        Define call-args as cast field-of on (said, 2).
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (said, 3)).
        // Named arguments first: everything after reads the arguments by position.
        Define passes-off as false.
        Define place as 4.
        While place is less than the number of said's children, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            Define marker as (item place of said's children)'s word.
            If marker is ":NamedArgs":
                The call-args becomes cast one's merged-arguments on (callee, call-args,
                    item (place + 1) of said's children, at-row) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            Otherwise if marker is ":PassesFailureOff":
                The passes-off becomes true.
            Done.
        Done.
        // A cast of an axiom runs it, and is checked against what the axiom takes.
        Define axiom-result as cast one's check-axiom-call on (callee, call-args, at-row, as-value, passes-off) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-none on (axiom-result) is false:
            If as-value, return axiom-result.
            Return cast unknown-type.
        Done.
        If callee's kind is "VariableReference":
            Define axiom-held as cast one's look-up on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (callee, 1))).
            If axiom-held is not void:
                If axiom-held's shape's kind is "AxiomType", return cast unknown-type.
            Done.
        Done.
        Define filled as cast one's call-filling on (said, callee, call-args, at-row) or pass the failure off.
        Define reached as cast one's resolve-cast on (callee, call-args, at-row, filled) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-none on (reached's shape), return reached's shape.
        Cast one's check-arguments on (reached, call-args, at-row) or pass the failure off.
        Define gives as cast field-of on (reached's shape, 2).
        Define display as reached's display.
        If as-value is false:
            If passes-off:
                Define passed as cast unknown-type.
                If cast is-nothing on (gives) is false, the passed becomes gives.
                Cast one's check-pass-off on (passed, display, at-row) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            Otherwise if one's in-try is false and cast is-nothing on (gives) is false:
                If cast is-failure-type on (gives):
                    Define fix as "Wrap this call in a 'Try to: / In case of failure:' block.".
                    If cast is-failure-type on (cast one's expected-return):
                        The fix becomes "Hand the failure to this function's caller — end the line '… or pass the failure off.' — or wrap the call in a 'Try to: / In case of failure:' block.".
                    Done.
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("{display} can fail — you must handle the failure", "",
                        at-row, "call a fallible function without handling the failure", fix)).
                Done.
            Done.
            Return cast unknown-type.
        Done.
        If cast is-nothing on (gives):
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("{display} gives nothing back — it can't be used as a value",
                "You declared it as void on line {reached's declared-on}", at-row, "use its result as a value",
                "Cast it as a statement instead, or change its return type if you need a result.")).
        Done.
        If cast is-void-or-failure on (gives):
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("{display} gives nothing back — it can't be used as a value",
                "You declared it as 'void or failure' on line {reached's declared-on}: it can fail, but when it works there is no result",
                at-row, "use its result as a value",
                "Cast it as a statement — inside 'Try to:', or ending '… or pass the failure off.' in a function that can fail.")).
        Done.
        If cast is-failure-type on (gives):
            If one's in-try, return cast field-of on (gives, 1).
            If one's handled is false:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("{display} can fail — you must handle the failure", "",
                    at-row, "use a fallible function's result without handling the failure",
                    "Wrap the call in a 'Try to: / In case of failure:' block, use 'but on failure <default>', or use 'or pass the failure off'.")).
            Done.
        Done.
        Return gives.
    Done.
Done.
